ently to forecast consumption and projected inventory needs; show the configured ratio and wastage-adjusted quantity used in each estimate.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Show demand and projected remaining inventory over daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, half-yearly, and annual horizons using available feeding plans and consumption history; flag projected stockouts and the relevant date or horizon.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Reject invalid quantities, units, or wastage ratios, and flag forecasts as incomplete when there is insufficient plan or usage data; do not silently treat missing data as zero demand.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-4\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Allow a user to create and edit a named ration with its type, intended animal or weight range, and ingredient quantities or proportions; calculate and display its blended cost per unit, dry-matter percentage, and energy value from its ingredients.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When an ingredient, proportion, or ingredient price changes, recalculate the ration's cost and nutritional totals and show the resulting values before the ration is used in a plan.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Let users compare eligible ration mixes by cost and nutritional values against specified animal or weight-range requirements, and show lower-cost candidates and the trade-offs against those requirements.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Prevent saving a ration with missing ingredients, invalid or negative amounts, or proportions that do not form a valid mix; identify unavailable or inactive ingredients instead of reporting a misleading cost or nutrition total.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-5\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Allow a user to generate or edit a dated feeding plan for a pen using its animal count, selected ration, bunk rate, and planned feeding time; show planned total feed, feed per animal, expected energy intake, and estimated feed cost.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Use the bunk rate as a daily feed quantity per animal; calculate the plan quantity from that rate and the pen's animal count, and allow the user to review or adjust the result before saving.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Support pens containing animals from multiple lots by recording the lot allocation used for the plan, so planned quantities and subsequent activity can be attributed to the appropriate lots.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Show plan status as Planned, In progress, Completed, or Skipped, and allow users to see plans by date and pen and identify plans without a ration, valid animal count, or bunk rate.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Do not generate a usable plan when the pen has no valid animal count, the ration is unavailable, or the bunk rate is invalid; explain the blocking condition.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"I interpret bunk rate as feed quantity per animal per day, so planned pen quantity is bunk rate multiplied by the pen's animal count.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-6\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Allow a user to record a dated feeding activity for a pen and lot allocation, including ration, planned quantity, actual delivered quantity, and feeding status; display the variance as actual minus planned quantity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On saving a valid activity, calculate its feed cost and energy from the ration and actual delivered quantity, allocate ingredient consumption according to the ration mix, apply configured wastage where